      "content": "# No-reasoning ablation (experiments/benchmarks/noreason, amendment 2): relabel-v2-long with the v2-noreason builder.\n# Relabel of all five v2 rubrics (experiments/benchmarks/relabel-v2) on ProgramBench's 13 long tasks (experiments/benchmarks/pls-relabel/subset_long.csv), whose\n# prompts are too long for one Read: same judge, reading in parts of 200 lines; the protocol check requires every prompt\n# line to come back. The other sets are in relabel-v2.toml.\n# Judge: Claude Code subagents, Opus 5.5 at effort low, v2 prompt.\n#   adele mass plan experiments/benchmarks/mass-annotation/specs/relabel-v2-long.toml\nname = \"noreason-long\"\n\n[tasks]\nbenchmarks = [\"programbench\"]\nsubset = \"experiments/benchmarks/pls-relabel/subset_long.csv\"\n\n[rubrics]\nrefs = [\"v2/PLp\", \"v2/PLe\", \"v2/PLs\", \"v2/MSm\", \"v2/MSc\"]\n\n[prompt]\nbuilder = \"v2-noreason\"\n\n[judge]\nbackend = \"subagent\"\nmodel = \"claude-opus-5-5\"\neffort = \"low\"\nrepeats = 1\nretry = { fallback_writer = 1, unparsed = 1 }\n\n[judge.relay]\ndispatcher = \"judge-dispatcher-v2-low-chunked\"\njudge_agent = \"adele-judge-v2-low-chunked\"\nmodel_alias = \"opus\"\nbatch_size = 100\nchunk_lines = 200\n"
